            "n_events": 31,
            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function. Here's how it works:\n\n**Key features:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrent tasks to `max_concurrent`\n- Handles `KeyboardInterrupt` gracefully:\n  - Catches the interrupt\n  - Cancels remaining tasks\n  - Waits for all tasks to finish (with `return_exceptions=True`) so cleanup code runs\n  - Re-raises the KeyboardInterrupt after cleanup completes\n\nThe implementation ensures that if a task has cleanup code (in `try/finally` blocks or `async with` context managers), it will run even when interrupted via Ctrl+C.\n\nYou can import and use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        # do work\n        pass\n    finally:\n        # cleanup will run even on KeyboardInterrupt\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2)\n```"
